From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: puffin <noreply@tlspuffin>
Date: Thu, 4 Sep 2026 17:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] client: bound the synchronous disconnect drain loop

disconnectSecureChannel(sync=true) spins `while(channel.state != CLOSED)
el->run(el,100)` with no bound. Under the in-process Puffin event loop a fuzzed
trace can leave the SecureChannel wedged in a non-CLOSED (even corrupted) state,
and el->run() always returns GOOD, so the loop never terminates -> a 30s+ silent
hang at agent teardown (UA_Client_disconnect and, transitively, UA_Client_delete)
that the fuzzer records as a Timeout objective. Cap the drain so teardown is
always bounded; a channel that has not closed after the cap is left to
notifyClientState as before.
---
 src/client/ua_client_connect.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/client/ua_client_connect.c b/src/client/ua_client_connect.c
index 0000000..1111111 100644
--- a/src/client/ua_client_connect.c
+++ b/src/client/ua_client_connect.c
@@ -2874,7 +2874,9 @@ disconnectSecureChannel(UA_Client *client, UA_Boolean sync) {
     if(sync && el &&
        el->state != UA_EVENTLOOPSTATE_FRESH &&
        el->state != UA_EVENTLOOPSTATE_STOPPED) {
-        while(client->channel.state != UA_SECURECHANNELSTATE_CLOSED) {
+        /* Puffin: bound the drain so a wedged/corrupted channel state cannot spin forever. */
+        size_t puffin_maxIters = 10000;
+        while(client->channel.state != UA_SECURECHANNELSTATE_CLOSED && puffin_maxIters-- > 0) {
             UA_StatusCode runStatus = el->run(el, 100);
             if(runStatus != UA_STATUSCODE_GOOD) {
                 UA_LOG_DEBUG(client->config.logging, UA_LOGCATEGORY_CLIENT,
